(* The syntax of the Wolfram Language

   The one place the Wolfram Language's syntax is written down. Wolfram/Parser's readers take their
   tables and their tokens from it: dev/freeze-syntax.wls reads its declarations with
   EBNFDeclarations, compiles its token rules to regular expressions, and writes both to
   WolframLanguageSyntax.wl, which the readers load, since they load no grammar reader; a test
   checks that the two agree, and another that the fast lexer's tokens span what the token rules
   read. It is a grammar in the classic dialect of EBNFRules, whose declarations are the lines that
   begin with %:

   %level name value
       a level that operators bind at, under the name CodeParser's Resources/Generated/Precedence.wl
       gives it. An operator of a higher level binds more tightly.

   %token spelling ...
       operators spelt in ASCII. An operator token is the longest of them at its place in the
       source: - is not read where ->, -- or -= is. Each is numbered in the reader's tables, in
       order, from 1.

   %longname operator name ...
       the long names an operator is also written as, as \[name] or as its character. An operator
       with no ASCII spelling is named by a word, and numbered after the tokens.

   %character character name ...
       the names CodeParser gives its tokens by, a name for each character: the token -> is
       Token`MinusGreater.

   %escape character text
       an escape of a string, a backslash and the character after it, and the text that stands
       for them, or its character code.

   %escapecode lead radix digits
       an escape of a string by a character code: a backslash, the lead and as many digits of
       the radix.

   %boxescape character code
       an escape of linear syntax, a backslash and the character after it, and the code of the
       character that stands for them. A backslash and a long name in brackets stand for its
       character.

   %space name ...
       the long names the front end reads as spaces besides those CodeParser does, which
       LongNameOperators.wl records, none of them a newline.

   %longhead name head
       the head a long-name operator of LongNameOperators.wl makes, where it is not its tag's,
       or for a relation its own name. CodeParser's table, which dev/freeze-longnames.wls
       records, gives the others: a relation is of the relations' chain, an InfixNode a chain
       of its tag, a BinaryNode a binary operator of its tag.

   %longform name form
       the form of a long-name operator the kernel reads otherwise than CodeParser's node says.

   %operator spelling level form head [chain key] [tag symbol]
       an operator: its spelling, the level it binds at, its form, and the head of the expression
       it makes. The forms:
           Prefix, Postfix     op a and a op: head[a]
           InfixL, InfixR      a op b, grouped from the left or from the right: head[a, b]
           InfixN              a op b op c: head[a, b, c], one expression for a run of the
                               operators of one level and one chain key, or of one operator
                               where it has no key; a - b in a sum is a + (-b)
           Ternary             a op f op b: f[a, b]
       and the forms with rules of their own:
           Call                f[a, ...], and f[[i, ...]]
           Derivative          f', f'' and so on
           MessageName         a::b::c, and t::[a, ...]
           Span                a ;; b ;; c, each operand optional
           Pattern             x:p, a name bound to a pattern
           Optional            p:v, a pattern with a default
           TagSet              t /: a = b, t /: a := b and t /: a =.
           Unset               a =. and a = ., a space between = and .
           Put                 a >> file and a >>> file
           Compound            a; b; c, each operand optional
       The spelling of a product is "", an operand right after an operand. The heads At,
       SlashSlash and NotNot are those of f @ a, a // f and !!a, which are f[a], f[a] and
       !(!a). tag is the head CodeParser gives the node, where it is not the head's own symbol.
       The rows are in the order of the reader's tables; a reader that takes the forms of one
       head with one rule, as the grammars do Unset's and Put's, takes the first.

   %tokens rule ...
       the rules of the tokens: names, numbers, strings, comments, whitespace and the rest. Each
       is read as a PEG reads it: its alternatives in order, the first that matches taken; an
       option and a repetition taking all they can and giving none back; &x and !x, where x
       must follow, or must not, taking nothing; and x - y, x where y does not match.
       dev/freeze-syntax.wls compiles each to regular expressions, which the readers make
       their parsers of.

   %class name range low high
   %class name reader
   %class name regex expression
       a class of characters no rule defines: those with codes from low to high; one the
       reader makes from its tables of long names; or those a regular expression matches.

   %check rule check
       a check of the text a token rule matched, past what the rule says, which the readers
       make: a token whose text fails it is none.
*)


(* Precedence *)

%level ColonColon             184
%level Infix`Question         178
%level Call                   176
%level Postfix`PlusPlus       174
%level Prefix`PlusPlus        172
%level AtStar                 170
%level SlashStar              168
%level At                     165
%level Tilde                  162
%level SlashAt                161
%level Postfix`Bang           158
%level SingleQuote            154
%level LessGreater            152
%level Caret                  151
%level StarStar               132
%level Dot                    126
%level Prefix`Minus           124
%level Slash                  122
%level Star                   108
%level Infix`Plus             86
%level SemiSemi               80
%level LongName`DirectedEdge  79
%level Class`Inequality       76
%level EqualEqualEqual        70
%level Class`SetRelations     68
%level Prefix`Bang            64
%level AmpAmp                 62
%level BarBar                 58
%level DotDot                 44
%level Bar                    42
%level Fake`PatternColon      40
%level Fake`OptionalColon     38
%level TildeTilde             36
%level SlashSemi              34
%level LessMinusGreater       33
%level MinusGreater           31
%level SlashDot               28
%level PlusEqual              27
%level Amp                    24
%level SlashSlashEqual        21
%level SlashSlash             18
%level SlashColon             11
%level Equal                  9
%level GreaterGreater         6
%level Semi                   4


(* Operator tokens *)

%token ">>>" "===" "=!=" "//@" "//." "//=" "@@@" "^:=" "..." "|->" "<->"
%token "->" ":>" ":=" "^=" "/:" "=." "==" "!=" "<=" ">=" "&&" "||" "<>" "/@" "@@" "@*" "/*" "//" "/." "/;" ".." "::"
%token "++" "--" "+=" "-=" "*=" "/=" ";;" "~~" "**" "!!" "<<" ">>" "<|" "|>"
%token "+" "-" "*" "/" "^" "=" "<" ">" "!" "&" "@" "?" ":" ";" "." "'" "~" "|"


(* Operators also written as long names *)

%longname "->"            Rule
%longname ":>"            RuleDelayed
%longname "*"             Times
%longname "=="            Equal LongEqual
%longname "!="            NotEqual
%longname "<="            LessEqual
%longname ">="            GreaterEqual
%longname "&&"            And
%longname "||"            Or
%longname "!"             Not
%longname "|->"           Function
%longname "<->"           TwoWayRule
%longname DirectedEdge    DirectedEdge
%longname UndirectedEdge  UndirectedEdge
%longname Element         Element


(* The characters CodeParser names its tokens by *)

%character "+" Plus        "-" Minus        "*" Star         "/" Slash       "^" Caret      "<" Less        ">" Greater
%character "=" Equal       ":" Colon        ";" Semi         "." Dot         "!" Bang       "@" At          "|" Bar
%character "&" Amp         "?" Question     "~" Tilde        "'" SingleQuote "_" Under      "#" Hash        "%" Percent
%character "," Comma       "[" OpenSquare   "]" CloseSquare  "{" OpenCurly   "}" CloseCurly "(" OpenParen   ")" CloseParen


(* String escapes *)

%escape "\r"   ""       (* a line continuation *)
%escape "\n"   ""
%escape "<"    ""       (* the ends of a string's boxes *)
%escape ">"    ""
%escape "\\"   92
%escape "\""   34
%escape "n"    10
%escape "t"    9
%escape "r"    13
%escape "b"    8
%escape "f"    12
%escape " "    32

%escapecode ""   8   3    (* \ooo *)
%escapecode "."  16  2    (* \.xx *)
%escapecode ":"  16  4    (* \:xxxx *)
%escapecode "|"  16  6    (* \|xxxxxx *)

%boxescape "!"  63425     (* U+F7C1 *)
%boxescape "("  63433     (* U+F7C9 *)
%boxescape ")"  63424     (* U+F7C0 *)
%boxescape "*"  63432     (* U+F7C8 *)
%boxescape "@"  63426     (* U+F7C2 *)
%boxescape "^"  63430     (* U+F7C6 *)
%boxescape "_"  63434     (* U+F7CA *)
%boxescape "%"  63429     (* U+F7C5 *)
%boxescape "&"  63431     (* U+F7C7 *)
%boxescape "+"  63435     (* U+F7CB *)
%boxescape "/"  63436     (* U+F7CC *)
%boxescape "`"  63437     (* U+F7CD *)


(* Spaces *)

%space COMPATIBILITYKanjiSpace DiscretionaryLineSeparator DiscretionaryParagraphSeparator


(* Long-name operators the kernel reads otherwise than CodeParser *)

%longhead LessSlantEqual        LessEqual
%longhead GreaterSlantEqual     GreaterEqual
%longhead HermitianConjugate    ConjugateTranspose
%longhead InvisibleApplication  At                  (* f \[InvisibleApplication] x is f[x] *)
%longform ImplicitPlus          InfixL              (* a sum of two, not a chain *)


(* Operators *)

%operator "::"            ColonColon             MessageName  MessageName
%operator "?"             Infix`Question         InfixL       PatternTest
%operator "["             Call                   Call         Call
%operator "++"            Postfix`PlusPlus       Postfix      Increment
%operator "--"            Postfix`PlusPlus       Postfix      Decrement
%operator "++"            Prefix`PlusPlus        Prefix       PreIncrement
%operator "--"            Prefix`PlusPlus        Prefix       PreDecrement
%operator "@*"            AtStar                 InfixN       Composition
%operator "/*"            SlashStar              InfixN       RightComposition
%operator "@"             At                     InfixR       At                      tag CodeParser`BinaryAt
%operator "~"             Tilde                  Ternary      Tilde
%operator "/@"            SlashAt                InfixR       Map
%operator "//@"           SlashAt                InfixR       MapAll
%operator "@@"            SlashAt                InfixR       Apply
%operator "@@@"           SlashAt                InfixR       MapApply
%operator "!"             Postfix`Bang           Postfix      Factorial
%operator "!!"            Postfix`Bang           Postfix      Factorial2
%operator "'"             SingleQuote            Derivative   Derivative
%operator "<>"            LessGreater            InfixN       StringJoin
%operator "^"             Caret                  InfixR       Power
%operator "**"            StarStar               InfixN       NonCommutativeMultiply
%operator "."             Dot                    InfixN       Dot
%operator "-"             Prefix`Minus           Prefix       Minus
%operator "+"             Prefix`Minus           Prefix       Plus
%operator "/"             Slash                  InfixL       Divide
%operator "*"             Star                   InfixN       Times                   chain Times
%operator ""              Star                   InfixN       Times                   chain Times
%operator "+"             Infix`Plus             InfixN       Plus                    chain Plus
%operator "-"             Infix`Plus             InfixN       Plus                    chain Plus
%operator ";;"            SemiSemi               Span         Span
%operator DirectedEdge    LongName`DirectedEdge  InfixR       DirectedEdge
%operator UndirectedEdge  LongName`DirectedEdge  InfixR       UndirectedEdge
%operator "=="            Class`Inequality       InfixN       Equal                   chain Relation  tag CodeParser`InfixInequality
%operator "!="            Class`Inequality       InfixN       Unequal                 chain Relation  tag CodeParser`InfixInequality
%operator "<="            Class`Inequality       InfixN       LessEqual               chain Relation  tag CodeParser`InfixInequality
%operator ">="            Class`Inequality       InfixN       GreaterEqual            chain Relation  tag CodeParser`InfixInequality
%operator "<"             Class`Inequality       InfixN       Less                    chain Relation  tag CodeParser`InfixInequality
%operator ">"             Class`Inequality       InfixN       Greater                 chain Relation  tag CodeParser`InfixInequality
%operator "==="           EqualEqualEqual        InfixN       SameQ
%operator "=!="           EqualEqualEqual        InfixN       UnsameQ
%operator Element         Class`SetRelations     InfixN       Element
%operator "!"             Prefix`Bang            Prefix       Not
%operator "!!"            Prefix`Bang            Prefix       NotNot                  tag CodeParser`PrefixNot2
%operator "&&"            AmpAmp                 InfixN       And
%operator "||"            BarBar                 InfixN       Or
%operator ".."            DotDot                 Postfix      Repeated
%operator "..."           DotDot                 Postfix      RepeatedNull
%operator "|"             Bar                    InfixN       Alternatives
%operator ":"             Fake`PatternColon      Pattern      Pattern
%operator ":"             Fake`OptionalColon     Optional     Optional
%operator "~~"            TildeTilde             InfixN       StringExpression
%operator "/;"            SlashSemi              InfixL       Condition
%operator "<->"           LessMinusGreater       InfixR       TwoWayRule
%operator "->"            MinusGreater           InfixR       Rule
%operator ":>"            MinusGreater           InfixR       RuleDelayed
%operator "/."            SlashDot               InfixL       ReplaceAll
%operator "//."           SlashDot               InfixL       ReplaceRepeated
%operator "+="            PlusEqual              InfixR       AddTo
%operator "-="            PlusEqual              InfixR       SubtractFrom
%operator "*="            PlusEqual              InfixR       TimesBy
%operator "/="            PlusEqual              InfixR       DivideBy
%operator "&"             Amp                    Postfix      Function
%operator "//="           SlashSlashEqual        InfixR       ApplyTo
%operator "//"            SlashSlash             InfixL       SlashSlash              tag CodeParser`BinarySlashSlash
%operator "/:"            SlashColon             TagSet       TagSet
%operator "= ."           Equal                  Unset        Unset
%operator "="             Equal                  InfixR       Set
%operator ":="            Equal                  InfixR       SetDelayed
%operator "^="            Equal                  InfixR       UpSet
%operator "^:="           Equal                  InfixR       UpSetDelayed
%operator "|->"           Equal                  InfixR       Function
%operator "=."            Equal                  Postfix      Unset
%operator ">>"            GreaterGreater         Put          Put
%operator ">>>"           GreaterGreater         Put          PutAppend
%operator ";"             Semi                   Compound     CompoundExpression


(* Tokens

   The tokens of a notebook's reading, which the held reader takes. A name is read whole, its
   context marks only between its parts: a` and a``b are none. A number is read as far as it
   goes, and its base checked after. *)

%tokens letter name digits number string comment blank slot out information_name freeform file unterminated_file
%tokens space line_space whitespace

%class character             range 0 1114111
%class held_letter_name      reader                    (* \[Name], a long name a notebook reads as a letter *)
%class held_letter_character reader                    (* a character past ASCII a notebook reads as a letter *)
%class held_space            reader                    (* a long name, or its character, a notebook reads as a space *)
%class held_newline          reader                    (* a long name, or its character, a notebook reads as a newline *)
%class unicode_letter        regex "[^\\P{L}\\x00-\\x7F]"   (* a letter past ASCII, as Unicode has it *)
%class end                   regex "\\z"              (* the end of the source *)

%check number base_digits     (* a base from 2 to 36, and only digits of the base after its ^^ *)

<letter>          ::= <held_letter_name> | <held_letter_character>
<ascii_letter>    ::= "a" | ... | "z" | "A" | ... | "Z"
<digit>           ::= "0" | ... | "9"
<alphanumeric>    ::= <digit> | <ascii_letter>

<name_start>      ::= <ascii_letter> | "$" | <letter>
<name_part>       ::= <name_start> { <name_start> | <digit> }
<name_character>  ::= <name_start> | <digit> | "`"
<name>            ::= [ "`" ] <name_part> { "`" <name_part> } ! <name_character>

<digits>          ::= <digit> { <digit> }
<number>          ::= <number_body> [ "`" [ "`" ] [ <precision> ] ] [ "*^" <exponent> ]
<number_body>     ::= <digits> [ "^^" <based_digits> | "." ! "." [ <digits> ] ] | "." <digits>
<based_digits>    ::= <alphanumeric> { <alphanumeric> } [ "." ! "." { <alphanumeric> } ] | "." <alphanumeric> { <alphanumeric> }
<precision>       ::= [ "-" | "+" ] ( <digits> [ "." ] { <digit> } | "." <digits> )
<exponent>        ::= [ "-" | "+" ] <digits>

<string>          ::= '"' { <character> - ( '"' | "\\" ) | "\\" <character> } '"'

(* a comment, the comments nested in it too; a backslash takes the ( after it, which opens none *)
<comment>         ::= "(*" { <comment> | <character> - ( "(" | "*" | "\\" ) | "\\" [ "(" ] | "(" ! "*" | "*" ! ")" } "*)"

<blank>           ::= "___" [ <name> ] | "__" [ <name> ] | "_" [ "." | <name> ]
<slot>            ::= "#" <string> | "##" { <digit> } | "#" [ <digits> | <slot_name> ]
<slot_name>       ::= ( <ascii_letter> | "$" | "`" ) { <ascii_letter> | <digit> | "$" | "`" }
<out>             ::= "%" { "%" } { <digit> }

(* what ? and ?? ask about: words of letters, digits and the * and @ of a name pattern, with the
   spaces and tabs between them *)
<information_character> ::= <alphanumeric> | "$" | "`" | "*" | "@"
<information_word> ::= ( <information_character> | <letter> ) { <information_character> | <letter> }
<information_name> ::= <information_word> { ( " " | "\t" ) { " " | "\t" } <information_word> }

(* free-form input: =[ and its text to the first ], the text on one line after any blank ones *)
<freeform>        ::= "=[" { " " | "\t" | "\r" | "\n" } { <character> - ( "]" | "\r" | "\n" ) }
                      [ ( "\r" | "\n" ) { " " | "\t" | "\r" | "\n" } ] "]"

(* the file of << and >>: a string, or the characters of a path or a context, a letter past ASCII
   and a \ among them, \[Name] one character, and brackets to their ] or the end of the source;
   and one whose \[ is not closed *)
<file>            ::= <string> | <file_unit> { <file_unit> }
<file_unit>       ::= <file_character> | <file_bracket>
<file_character>  ::= <alphanumeric> | "$" | "`" | "_" | "." | "/" | "~" | ":" | "!" | "*" | "?" | "-" | <unicode_letter>
                    | "\\[" <alphanumeric> { <alphanumeric> } "]" | "\\" ! "["
<file_bracket>    ::= "[" { <character> - ( "[" | "]" ) | <file_bracket> } ( "]" | <end> )
<unterminated_file> ::= { <file_character> } "\\[" { <alphanumeric> } ! "]"

(* whitespace: a space, a tab, a form feed, a line continued, a comment or a long name a notebook
   reads as a space; on a line, or across lines *)
<space>           ::= " " | "\t" | "\f" | "\\\n" | "\\\r\n" | <comment> | <held_space>
<line_space>      ::= { <space> }
<whitespace>      ::= { "\n" | "\r" | <held_newline> | <space> }


(* The tokens of CodeParser's reading, which the concrete reader takes. A name's parts are joined
   by single context marks, and a ` after a name that no part follows is CodeParser's
   Token`Error`ExpectedLetterlike. A number's text is read as far as a number could go: the reader
   makes Token`Error`Number of a text no number has. *)

%tokens concrete_name letterlike_error number_text unterminated_string unterminated_comment
%tokens unhandled_character concrete_comment concrete_blanks concrete_newline

%class concrete_letter_name      reader    (* \[Name], a long name CodeParser reads as a letter *)
%class concrete_letter_character reader    (* a character past ASCII CodeParser reads as a letter *)
%class unknown_long_name         reader    (* \[Name], a long name that is not CodeParser's *)

<concrete_letter>      ::= <concrete_letter_name> | <concrete_letter_character>
<ascii_part>           ::= ( <ascii_letter> | "$" ) { <ascii_letter> | <digit> | "$" }
<ascii_name_character> ::= <ascii_letter> | <digit> | "$"
<concrete_part_start>  ::= <ascii_letter> | "$" | <concrete_letter>
<concrete_name>        ::= ( <ascii_part> { "`" <ascii_part> } | "`" <ascii_part> { "`" <ascii_part> }
                           | [ "`" ] <concrete_letter> { <ascii_name_character> } )
                           { <concrete_letter> { <ascii_name_character> } | "`" <concrete_part_start> { <ascii_name_character> } }
<letterlike_error>     ::= [ <concrete_name> ] "`" ! <concrete_part_start>

<signed_digits>        ::= [ "-" | "+" ] ( <digits> [ "." [ <digits> ] ] | "." <digits> )
<number_text>          ::= ( <digits> [ "^^" { <alphanumeric> } [ "." ! "." { <alphanumeric> } ] | "." ! "." [ <digits> ] ] | "." <digits> )
                           [ "`" [ "`" ] [ <signed_digits> ] ] [ "*^" [ [ "-" | "+" ] <digits> ] ]

(* a string or a comment the source does not close: the rest of the source *)
<unterminated_string>  ::= '"' { <character> }
<unterminated_comment> ::= "(*" { <character> }

(* a \ that begins no letter, CodeParser's Token`Error`UnhandledCharacter: a long name not the
   language's, a \[ not closed, a \: \. \| short of its digits, or a \ and the character after it,
   none at the end *)
<hex_digit>            ::= <digit> | "a" | ... | "f" | "A" | ... | "F"
<unhandled_character>  ::= <unknown_long_name> | "\\[" { <alphanumeric> } ! "]"
                         | "\\:" [ <hex_digit> [ <hex_digit> [ <hex_digit> ] ] ] ! <hex_digit>
                         | "\\." [ <hex_digit> ] ! <hex_digit>
                         | "\\|" [ <hex_digit> [ <hex_digit> [ <hex_digit> [ <hex_digit> [ <hex_digit> ] ] ] ] ] ! <hex_digit>
                         | "\\" ! ( "[" | ":" | "." | "|" | "\n" | "\r" ) [ <character> ]

(* a comment, the comments nested in it too, as CodeParser reads it: a backslash takes nothing *)
<concrete_comment>     ::= "(*" { <concrete_comment> | <character> - ( "(" | "*" ) | "(" ! "*" | "*" ! ")" } "*)"
<concrete_blanks>      ::= ( " " | "\t" ) { " " | "\t" }
<concrete_newline>     ::= "\r\n" | "\n" | "\r"
